{
  "_about": [
    "Listen mood config (PROJECT-SPEC.md §7). The page renders the selector, turntable, and now spinning bar from this file plus content/listen/mood-words.json.",
    "Each mood's descriptor, blurb, description, and Sarah's Picks live in content/listen/mood-words.json (editable in the CMS), matched by id. This file is not in the CMS.",
    "live: true shows the mood in the selector; false hides it completely (not shown as locked). Going live later = flip it to true.",
    "UNDECIDED = not decided by Sarah yet; the page shows nothing for it rather than inventing copy.",
    "PLACEHOLDER = no real URL yet. With no Apple Music URL, the Spotify / Apple Music toggle is hidden for that mood (launch is Spotify-only); it appears once a real URL is added.",
    "Array order is the current display order. Final display order is UNDECIDED; the number on each label is its position among the live moods.",
    "labelText: text color on the circle art (dark or light), for contrast. labelShadow: true adds a faint dark shadow behind that text, for circle art where neither text color reaches 4.5:1 on its own (the red circle).",
    "titleColor: optional text color for the mood name on its tape banner (any CSS color). Leave it out to use the default near-black. Keep at least 3:1 contrast against the banner.",
    "labelColors hex values are PROVISIONAL, sampled from the circle art; final hex values are UNDECIDED.",
    "art paths are the existing assets (circles are 320px WebP exports; full-size originals in archive/listen-circle-originals/). Each live mood uses one color's full set (circle, vinyl, record, tape) plus that color's labelColors entry, never mixed. Non-live moods with color UNDECIDED keep the art they had, so some share art with a live mood; Hopeful / Hypnotic use forest green / silver art even though the spec leaves their colors open. art.record is the pre-composited record export, not currently rendered.",
    "selectorNote: short note shown near the selector (e.g. that more moods are coming). UNDECIDED = nothing shown; wording and style are Sarah's call."
  ],
